course: dictionary
lesson: 5755
title: Being loyal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Loyal is an adjective. It describes someone who always supports and cares about a friend, family, team or country, and does not let them down. In «The loyal Mole agrees», the word loyal tells you the Mole stays on his friend's side.
explain: Look at the words around loyal to work out its meaning. «With his son and loyal helpers, drove them out.» Odysseus's helpers stayed with him and helped him when it mattered. Check your meaning by swapping in "faithful and supportive": the sentence still makes sense, so loyal must mean that.
explain: Loyal often goes with "to", as in loyal to a friend. Its noun is loyalty. A loyal friend stays by you, and a loyal friend does not let you down, even when it is hard.
explain: Being loyal can sometimes clash with other good things. «A dilemma is a choice where two good things pull in different directions, such as being honest and being loyal to a friend.» Choosing between two good things is a dilemma, and you have to think carefully about what to do.
fact: Loyal means always supporting and caring about a friend, family, team or country, and not letting them down.
fact: Loyal is an adjective. Its noun is loyalty.
fact: Loyal can be followed by "to", as in «loyal to a friend».
fact: In stories, a loyal companion stays with the hero to the end.
fact: Dogs are often called loyal because they stay close to the people they care about.
exercise: «The loyal Mole agrees» shows that the Mole is | Quiet and shy | *Always supporting his friend | Bored of his friends | Late for tea
exercise: «With his son and loyal helpers, drove them out.» Who were the loyal helpers? | Men who were feasting in his hall | Men who wanted to marry Penelope | *Men who stayed with Odysseus and helped him | Beggars who wanted food
exercise: Which word is the noun from loyal? | Lawful | Royal | Loyal | *Loyalty
test:
«Sam had been his mate since nursery.» A loyal mate is someone who | Forgets you when you are sad | *Stays by you and does not let you down | Only plays when it suits them | Tells everyone your secrets
test:
Which is most likely to be a loyal friend? | Tell your secrets to everyone at school | Leave you alone when you need help | *Stand up for you when others are unkind | Laugh when you get hurt
exam: Which phrase uses loyal correctly? | a loyal lunch box | *a loyal friend who stays by you | loyal rain falls fast | the loyal number seven
